/-!
# Equations 18–24 from the zeroth inverse conjugate

Bounded collection with the original SylowNormalEights relations.
The candidate lists are generated by ZeroPairs/source/generate.py;
each collection identity is checked by the Lean kernel.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith A.3.12, pp.47–48; see ZeroPairs/source/README.md.

Both orders of each selected pair are collected in the original group.
Full cardinality makes their Boolean coordinates unique, so actual
commutation forces the seven coordinate differences to vanish.
The common conjugate identities remain an explicit premise for the parent.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter1.Terminal.LinearFourActions.JankoFourStabilizer.Max1Placement.SylowCover.OutsideKernelOrders.AbstractCatalogue.Localization.GroupTests
open PointwiseCalculation Symbolic

open Janko4.LocalStructure.SylowNormalEights Presentation

/-- The four selected pairs involving the zeroth conjugate force equations 18–24.
The common conjugate collection premise is discharged by the assembly owner. -/
theorem zeroPairTests (hcard : Nat.card Carrier = 2^21) (hconj : CollectedConjugates) :
    ConjugateTestsBetween 18 25 := by
  intro b hc i hlo hhi
  have hi : i = 18 ∨ i = 19 ∨ i = 20 ∨ i = 21 ∨ i = 22 ∨ i = 23 ∨ i = 24 := by omega
  rcases hi with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
  · exact ZeroPairs.test18 hcard hconj b hc
  · exact ZeroPairs.test19 hcard hconj b hc
  · exact ZeroPairs.test20 hcard hconj b hc
  · exact ZeroPairs.test21 hcard hconj b hc
  · exact ZeroPairs.test22 hcard hconj b hc
  · exact ZeroPairs.test23 hcard hconj b hc
  · exact ZeroPairs.test24 hcard hconj b hc

end CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter1.Terminal.LinearFourActions.JankoFourStabilizer.Max1Placement.SylowCover.OutsideKernelOrders.AbstractCatalogue.Localization.GroupTests
